{"kind":"report","text":"Approved exact head 9c663be7b3e031880df8e5f3e9998214ee6f4f19, all nine published paths. No blocking findings.\n\nArchitecture: layers 4 (application boundary), 5 (interpreter) and 7 (command composition) retain their contracts in docs/reference/architecture.md@9c663be7b3e031880df8e5f3e9998214ee6f4f19. Deferred public rendering and a separate admission projection change when work is paid, not what the projection means. The admission cache is private to one workspace/interpreter and keyed by its verified head. Its check callback still runs on every submission. The receipt-plan memo belongs to one staleness pass, uses the exact receipt identity and stores read-only narrowed plans. No protocol, profile or architecture-contract change requires a new architecture artifact.\n\nSecurity: verified reading, actor and sequencer signatures, post-dedup admission and sequence-ref compare-and-swap remain authoritative. Admission consumes newly read events before refusing a mismatched head, so a later retry cannot silently lose them. Skipping the undefined-kind warning applies only to newly admitted acts; replay retains the check. Empty published paths do not lend a receipt plan. No unresolved trust or authority defect found. The extra retained admission projection and reader contention are disclosed; this is no bound on resident memory or end-to-end landing latency.\n\nSimplification: the shared render helper and per-pass memo remove repeated work without adding policy. A persistent cross-pass cache would complicate invalidation and is unnecessary. No fluff to cut as a condition of approval.\n\nIndependent verification at the exact head: go test -timeout 40m ./internal/app ./internal/workroom ./cmd/gs ./cmd/gitseq-mcp passed (160.902 s, 6.840 s, 563.790 s and 67.920 s); targeted app admission/deferred-render race tests passed (7.138 s); go vet on the four affected packages and git diff --check passed. Read the author's full-suite output: 36 packages passed